X86_64 Ticketlock3
(* Ticket lock on x86-TSO (see ticketlock2.kl): `lock xadd` on `next`,
   plain-load spin on `owner`, release with a plain store of owner+1
   (the other release idiom; ticketlock2.kl uses `incl`). Three threads
   each increment a shared counter once.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state.
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (rule-level):
   `TicketX.ticket3_counter_envG_runner_noFault`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64NoFaultDLocks.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t`) so that the runner declares
   them as sized locations at the width of the code's accesses (DECLS,
   typed .kl symbols): the runner's declarations then agree with the
   proofs' locations. The code block and the verdict are unchanged.
   Proved: TicketX.ticket3_counter_envG_verbatim and
   TicketX.ticket3_counter_envG_runner (EnvG/TicketXPublic.lean), with
   the runner-exact instance in EnvG/TicketXRunner.lean.
   Proved (fault freedom at the runner's declarations, MEMVALS):
   `TicketX.ticket3_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/X64FaultFreeFixed.lean), with a `.Concrete` instance.
   Proved (LIVEX64A): promise-free liveness (every waiting thread is
   eventually done, under WeakFair and MemFair, valid layouts)
   `Live.TicketX64PF.ticket3_x64_live_pf`, with
   `ticket3_x64_live_pf_concrete` at the runner's layout
   (Promising/LiveX64TicketPF.lean); weak fairness alone is not enough:
   `Live.TicketX64Cex.ticketX64LiveWF_false` (Promising/LiveX64TicketCex.lean).
   With promises (LIVEX64SEM): proved on the machine with semantic
   certification, for every fuel, valid layouts:
   `Live.X64SemTicket.ticket3_x64_live_sem`, with
   `ticket3_x64_live_sem_concrete` at the runner's layout
   (Promising/LiveX64SemTicket.lean); the statement over `succs`
   stays open (`certify` is incomplete; KNOWN_GAPS "Liveness: ticket
   lock, x64").
# flags: -sym -fuel 300
# expect: Always
*)
{
uint32_t next=0; uint32_t owner=0; uint32_t counter=0;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  movl $1,%eax
  lock xaddl %eax,(next)
spin:
  movl (owner),%ecx
  cmpl %eax,%ecx
  jne spin
  movl (counter),%edx
  addl $1,%edx
  movl %edx,(counter)
  addl $1,%ecx
  movl %ecx,(owner)
  jmp done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
